    "Many workers in Pakistan only start thinking about their legal rights after something goes wrong. Salary is delayed. Overtime is ignored. A worker is forced to resign. A female employee is pressured during pregnancy. An injured worker is abandoned. A long-serving employee is removed without proper process. That is usually the moment panic starts.\n\nThe hard truth is simple. By the time many employees seek legal advice, the employer has already shaped the record. Messages have gone missing. Attendance proof is unclear. Salary arrangements were verbal. Appointment terms were never reviewed. The worker knows an injustice happened, but proving it becomes harder than it should have been.\n\nThat is why this issue matters now, not later. A worker who understands his or her rights early stands on stronger legal ground than a worker who waits until the situation becomes unbearable.",

