    "Employee rights in Pakistan are not limited to one single right or one single law. They form a broader legal framework that can include fair wages, regulated hours, weekly or annual rest and leave, maternity-related protection, social security, workplace safety, old-age benefits, industrial relations, and protection from arbitrary or unlawful employer conduct.\n\nIn practical terms, a worker’s rights are shaped by several factors at once. These include whether the person is employed in a factory, office, shop, commercial establishment, industrial undertaking, domestic setting, or another category, and whether the matter falls under federal or provincial law.\n\nThis is where confusion starts. Employees often hear broad statements like 'You have no rights' or 'This is company policy.' In law, neither of those sentences settles the matter. The real question is, which statute applies, what documents exist, what forum has jurisdiction, and what remedy can realistically be claimed.",

