  mistakesTitle: "Common Mistakes and Legal Risks",
  commonMistakesAndRisks:
    "The first major mistake is choosing a weak or descriptive mark. Businesses often prefer names that merely describe the product or praise the quality, but legally those can be harder to protect.\n\nThe second mistake is filing without proper clearance. Many businesses assume that if a domain name or social media handle is available, the mark must also be legally safe. That assumption is dangerous.\n\nAnother common mistake is filing in the wrong class or too few classes. A business may protect one category while leaving commercially important areas exposed.\n\nBusinesses also make avoidable errors by delaying filing, using different versions of the mark inconsistently, failing to monitor competitors, ignoring opposition risks, and assuming that registration alone automatically stops infringement.\n\nThe legal and commercial risks include refusal, opposition, infringement disputes, loss of exclusivity, brand dilution, forced rebranding, distributor misuse, customer confusion, licensing problems, and expensive litigation.",

