    "From a legal strategy point of view, the smartest tax filer is not the one who files fastest. It is the one whose documents, disclosures, and explanations can survive future scrutiny.\n\nFor individuals, the key issue is usually not only taxable income. It is whether your declared record can support your real financial profile. For businesses, the issue is whether the return is consistent with books, banking, contracts, and operational history.\n\nOne of the most common legal errors is treating tax filing as a one-time data entry task. In truth, every return becomes part of a longer narrative. If that narrative is weak, inconsistent, or careless, it may create problems later in notices, audits, banking questions, or litigation.\n\nA careful lawyer or tax adviser will always look beyond the filed figure. He will ask whether the filing position is sustainable.",

