    "The first and most common mistake is confusing one document with another. A birth certificate is not the same thing as CRC, and CRC is not the same thing as CNIC or NICOP.\n\nThe second mistake is delay. Many families postpone child registration, assuming it can be fixed easily later. Later is usually more difficult because documents, memories, family linkage, and supporting records become harder to align.\n\nAnother common mistake is inconsistent identity data, including spelling differences, date-of-birth discrepancies, incomplete family linkage, or unclear supporting documents. These issues can trigger referral, further scrutiny, or repeated visits.\n\nApplicants also make mistakes by assuming that everything can be done online. NADRA’s own Pak Identity FAQs make clear that not every category is available online, especially for fresh Smart ID cases.\n\nThe risks include delayed school admissions, passport and visa problems, family record mismatch, travel disruption, banking difficulty, inheritance documentation issues, and prolonged identity verification problems.",

