  mistakesTitle: "Common Mistakes and Legal Risks",
  commonMistakesAndRisks:
    "The first big mistake is using generic documents for every country. A UK visitor file, a Canada file, and a Schengen file may overlap, but they are not identical in structure or expectation.\n\nThe second mistake is exaggeration. Overstated income, artificial bank balances, weakly explained sponsorship, or inflated business claims can quietly destroy credibility.\n\nAnother common mistake is confusing invitation with approval. An invitation letter can help, but it does not replace the applicant’s own duty to prove purpose, finances, and return intention.\n\nPeople also make avoidable errors by submitting unread agent-prepared applications, using inconsistent travel dates, giving unclear job or business evidence, or hiding prior refusals instead of addressing them honestly.\n\nThe risks include refusal, future scrutiny, weak credibility in later applications, wasted travel plans, and in serious cases allegations of misrepresentation or unreliable documentation.",

