  mistakesTitle: "Common Mistakes and Legal Risks",
  commonMistakesAndRisks:
    "The first major mistake is buying a policy without first identifying the actual risk. Many people buy what sounds attractive, not what solves their problem.\n\nThe second mistake is focusing only on premium and ignoring terms. A cheap premium can hide weak cover, narrow benefit triggers, long exclusions, or unsatisfactory claims experience.\n\nAnother common mistake is treating an agent’s verbal explanation as the full legal position. The enforceable reality lies in the policy wording, exclusions, declarations, and claim requirements.\n\nPolicyholders also make avoidable mistakes by failing to disclose material facts, not updating records, misunderstanding nomination issues, missing premium continuity requirements, or assuming that maturity or claim benefits are automatic regardless of documentation.\n\nThe risks include claim disputes, underinsurance, unexpected exclusions, lapsed policies, poor family protection, financial disappointment, and avoidable litigation or complaint escalation.",

