  practicalApplication:
    "In real life, courtroom representation usually includes several separate layers.\n\nThe lawyer studies the facts and documents.\nThe correct legal forum is identified.\nThe main pleading, application, reply, or petition is drafted.\nInterim relief is considered where needed.\nFiling, objections, and procedural compliance are managed.\nHearing dates are tracked through the court system.\nArguments are advanced in stages depending on what the case needs.\nOrders are obtained, interpreted, and acted upon.\n\nA client may only see the hearing itself, but the hearing is often the visible tip of a much larger legal process.",

