    "A lot of businesses in Pakistan only start thinking seriously about sales tax when one of three things happens. A buyer demands a proper tax invoice. A supplier asks for a registration number. Or FBR starts asking questions.\n\nBy that stage, the business is often already exposed. Pricing may have been done without tax logic. Input and output records may be weak. Invoices may be inconsistent. Purchases and supplies may no longer line up cleanly with the legal position the business now wants to claim.\n\nThat is why sales tax registration matters. It is not just about obtaining a number. It is about entering a compliance structure that affects invoicing, filing, record discipline, pricing, and tax exposure from the moment the business starts operating in the relevant category.",

